{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1199024-cybernetic-augmentations-good-as-they-sound","id":1199024,"title":"Cybernetic augmentations - Good as they sound?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-03-24T06:46:04-07:00","id":1199024,"title":"Cybernetic augmentations - Good as they sound?","content":"I LOVE cybernetic augmentations, maybe because i'm a tehno freak or just really don't like the &quot;stock&quot; limbs I have but I really love making things more machine, now I'm not sure how good are they compared to their counterparts with no augmentations.<br /> <br /> Say you turn a Garou into a Weaver monster of metal and flesh, would that actually be able to negate the weakness if you shield his body in steel or a vampire in that case, for humans i wonder, can we go beyond 5 attributes if we are going all out machine or cyborg?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23861-phantomdragenoid","name":"PhantomDragenoid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23861_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-24T07:24:27-07:00","id":1199042,"title":"","content":"For humans yes, it is a cheat to go beyond 5 in Attributes, how depends on the system. I like to mix the Strike Force Zero rules with the Book of the Weaver rules.<br /> <br /> It gets messier for many supernaturals though particularly Vampires who would need some sort of magic to let their body accept the graft, but it would be a cool theme for a blood sorcery ritual. Werewolves have a lot of social as well as physiological restrictions. Culturally even their most Weaver Friendly tribe the Glasswalkers just had to purge a camp of Cyborgs because they went overboard, with the other tribes you would very much be distrusted and loose honer the more extravagant you go.<br /> <br /> For mages, its even better then for humans!<br /> <br /> For Changelings I would imagine it would be a heavy source of banality unless it was some sort of chimerical hardwire like House Dougal's artificial limbs, or a Treasure limb, which would probably look like crap to those who are not enchanted.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-24T08:30:00-07:00","id":1199069,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PhantomDragenoid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1199024-cybernetic-augmentations-good-as-they-sound#post1199024\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I LOVE cybernetic augmentations, maybe because i'm a tehno freak or just really don't like the &quot;stock&quot; limbs I have but I really love making things more machine, now I'm not sure how good are they compared to their counterparts with no augmentations.<br /> <br /> Say you turn a Garou into a Weaver monster of metal and flesh, would that actually be able to negate the weakness if you shield his body in steel or a vampire in that case, for humans i wonder, can we go beyond 5 attributes if we are going all out machine or cyborg?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Creatures with regenerative powers such as Werewolves and Vampires may have a difficult time installing the implants. A vampire's body tries to restore itself back to the state it was in at the time of its death while they sleep through the day, while Werewolves are capable of rapidly growing back severed body parts.<br /> <br /> <br /> The Changelings of House Dougal have a tendency (or at least they used to) for replacing their body parts with artificial enhancements. But these were largely chimerical in nature.<br /> <br /> <br /> I think the most obvious supernatural to pull it off would be Mages, having found some way to combine magic and technology together to create a functional prosthetic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 03-24-2018, 11:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-24T10:52:14-07:00","id":1199115,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PhantomDragenoid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1199024-cybernetic-augmentations-good-as-they-sound#post1199024\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">for humans i wonder, can we go beyond 5 a